#: contactMatrix.md:1
msgid "Contact matices and coordination numbers"
msgstr ""

#: contactMatrix.md:3
msgid ""
"The $i$, $j$ element of the conntact matrix, $\\mathbf{C}_{ij}$, is one if "
"atoms $i$ and $j$ are within a certain distance $r_c$ of each other and zero"
" otherwise. Consequently, if $\\mathbf{C}$ is multiplied from the back by a "
"vector of ones the $i$th element of the resulting matrix tells you the "
"number of atoms that are within $r_c$ of atom $i$. In other words, the "
"coordination numbers of the atoms can be calculated from the contact matrix "
"by doing matrix vector multiplication."
msgstr ""

#: contactMatrix.md:7
msgid ""
"This realisation about the relationship between the contact map and the "
"coordination number is heavily used in the new version of PLUMED. For "
"example, to calculate and print the coordination numbers of the first 7 "
"atoms in the system with themselves you would use an input something like "
"this:"
msgstr ""

#: contactMatrix.md:17
msgid ""
"Implmenting the coordination number this way is useful as there are many "
"different ways to define whether two atoms/molecules and to construct a "
"\"contact\" matrix based on the result. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: contactMatrix.md:20
msgid ""
"You could say that two molecules are connected if they are within a certain "
"distance of each other and if they have the same orientation."
msgstr ""

#: contactMatrix.md:21
msgid ""
"You could say that two water molecules are connected if they are hydrogen "
"bonded to each other."
msgstr ""

#: contactMatrix.md:22
msgid ""
"You could say that two atoms are connected if they are within a certain "
"distance of each other and if they have similar values for a CV."
msgstr ""

#: contactMatrix.md:24
msgid ""
"When the coordination numbers is implemented in the way described above (by "
"doing the matrix-vector multiplication) you have the flexibility to define "
"the contact matrix that is used in the multiplication in whatever way you "
"choose. In other words, the newer implementation of the coordination number "
"is much more flexible."
msgstr ""

